    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The spread is this lesson's own fact. The dots run from "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·9",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " at the bottom to "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·13",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " at the top — five frets, not four — and fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "11",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " holds nothing at all. They sit on frets "
        },
        {
          "text": "9",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "12",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "13",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", with a gap through the middle. If you can't reach the whole thing in one hand position, you're reading the shape right, not failing it. It isn't the only window that spreads, either: the "
        },
        {
          "text": "G form",
          "marks": ["italic"]
        },
        {
          "text": " does the same thing further down the neck."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "tip",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fret 11 is empty. This window is two small clusters — 9/10 and 12/13 — not one hand position."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The two clusters aren't identical in content, either. The lower one, frets 9–10, holds the root at "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " alongside the "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " at "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". The upper one, frets 12–13, holds the other root at "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·12",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " alongside the "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " at "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·13",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Each cluster already carries a root and a "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " of its own, so neither is a leftover from the other — you could sit in either one and still hear the chord."
        }
      ]
    },
